# Pub Menu Architecture

## Purpose

- This is the fast architecture context file for the agent.
- Detailed requirements and architecture live in `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Structural history lives in `docs/architecture/CHANGELOG.md`.

## Mandatory Read Order (structural tasks)

1. User request
2. This file (`.cursor/rules/architecture.mdc`)
3. `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md`
4. Minimal additional files required by the task

## Core Boundaries

- Multi-tenant data isolation is enforced in DB (Supabase + RLS).
- Domain/API logic belongs in `apps/web/src/lib/services` and `packages/db`, not page components.
- Components stay small and feature-focused; split by responsibility early.
- Prefer extending existing domain services over introducing duplicate fetch/request flows.
- Admin Web App (`/admin/*`) is a mandatory product surface and must remain in implementation scope.

## Structural Change Triggers

Update architecture docs in the same task when you change:

- DB schema/migrations/RLS/auth data model
- service boundaries or domain ownership
- route/layout structure
- shared package/module boundaries

## Sync Checklist

- Update date and impacted sections in `docs/architecture/ARCHITECTURE.md`
- Append one entry to `docs/architecture/CHANGELOG.md` (`date | change | reason`)
- Keep this file aligned if global boundaries/policy changed
